# Aston Martin DB6 fixed-head coupe, 1965-1970.
#
# The DB6, the DB5's body with a longer wheelbase, a higher roofline and a Kamm
# tail, on sale from 1965 to 1970. The fixed-head coupe is modelled, not the
# Volante convertible.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB6 (infobox, with the wheelbase
# attributed to the Daily Express Review of the 1966 Motor Show)
#
# Dimensions 4.6228 x 1.6764 x 1.3589 m, wheelbase 2.5781 m, converted from the
# pack's 182 x 66 x 53.5 in and 101.5 in figures. The hull measures 4.6228 m on
# the 2.5781 m wheelbase (55.8 per cent), 1.6764 m wide and 1.3589 m high.
#
# Shape reference: the pack is **not one car** — the side view is a green 1965
# Mk I and both three-quarter views are a red 1966 coupe — and the notes say so
# image by image. The side view governs the flank and roof line; the front
# three-quarter the grille, the split bumper and the headlamps; the rear the
# Kamm tail with its flat cut-off and upturned lip.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found (grade d); cars of this era
# were finished to order, so the objects carry plain names: British Racing
# Green, silver, black and red. Weights green 3, silver 3, black 2, red 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h, the DB6 Vantage's quoted maximum. Comfort 65/280, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 65: more spacious than the DB5 thanks to the longer wheelbase and
# the raised roof. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1965 intro, retires staggered 1980-1983 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db6.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db6.dae (62 objects). References:
# citycars/references/aston-db6/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the lower wheel-arch transitions are more angular than
# the photographed car's, and the three-way camera match is approximate. All
# glazing stands 14.4-15.0 mm clear of its supporting surfaces. At 128 px the
# higher roofline, the split bumper and the flat Kamm tail read as a DB6.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDB6(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1965
intro_month=1
retire_year=1983
retire_month=6
speed=240
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=280

